> No, this is right. Gray stones and rocks are both "stones" if you
> haven't seen them or have only seen them at a distance; in source
> terms, if the dknown flag isn't set on them. Blessed object detection
> or skilled detect treasure is considered as seeing the items it finds
> as close-up; uncursed/unskilled as at a distance.

s/skilled/skilled or expert/

s/unskilled/unskilled or basic/

> What may be confusing you is that breaking boulders or statues
> _doesn't_ unset the dknown flag, and they have it set for them by
> default (since they don't have any more specific description to be
> known; the nature of a statue is presumed to be obvious from a
> distance or by feel). Hence, breaking an unseen boulder results in seen
> rocks. This is very probably a bug; I'll ask the DevTeam.

That explains my test. I din't bother to answer as my wizmode test 
